Rule 11 lists these minor penalties [(Rule 11, PDF p. 10)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=10):

- (i) censure;
- (ii) withholding of promotion;
- (iii) recovery from pay of the whole or part of any loss caused to the Government by negligence or breach of orders;
- (iii a) reduction to a lower stage in the time-scale of pay by one stage for up to three years, without cumulative effect and without adversely affecting pension;
- (iv) withholding of increments of pay.

The major penalties are [(Rule 11, PDF p. 10)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=10) [(Rule 11, PDF p. 11)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=11):

- (v) reduction to a lower stage in the time-scale of pay for a specified period, with directions on increments during and after the period;
- (vi) reduction to a lower time-scale, grade, post or Service for a specified period, which bars promotion back during that period;
- (vii) compulsory retirement;
- (viii) removal from service, which is not a disqualification for future Government employment;
- (ix) dismissal from service, which is ordinarily a disqualification for future Government employment.

If a charge of disproportionate assets, or of accepting illegal gratification as a motive or reward for an official act, is established, the penalty must be removal or dismissal. Another penalty can be imposed only in an exceptional case, for special reasons recorded in writing [(Rule 11, provisos, PDF p. 11)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=11).

The Explanation to Rule 11 says some actions are not penalties [(Rule 11, Explanation, PDF p. 11)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=11). These include:

- withholding increments for failing a required departmental examination;
- stopping you at the efficiency bar because you are unfit to cross it;
- not promoting you after your case has been considered;
- reverting you from an officiating post because you are unsuitable or for administrative reasons unconnected with your conduct.

Compulsory retirement under the superannuation or retirement rules, and termination of a probationer or temporary employee under the terms of appointment, are also not penalties [(Rule 11, Explanation (vii)-(viii), PDF p. 12)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=12).
